.Dd October 10, 2026
.Dt LID-SWITCHD 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm lid-switchd
.Nd ACPI lid-switch policy and suspend helper
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm Cm start
.Nm Cm stop
.Nm Cm status
.Nm Cm serve
.Nm Cm awake
.Nm Cm s0ix
.Nm Cm s3
.Nm Cm toggle
.Nm Cm suspend-s0ix
.Nm Cm suspend-s3
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the root helper for sysctl
.Va hw.acpi.lid_switch_state .
The rc script starts it with
.Cm serve ,
after
.Pa /etc/rc.d/sysctl
has run.
.Pp
At start the daemon reads the running
.Xr sysctl 3
value of
.Va hw.acpi.lid_switch_state
and does not change it.
It does not read
.Xr sysctl.conf 5
or
.Xr rc.conf 5
for that value.
The sysctl boot value is whatever the
.Cm sysctl
service already applied, usually from
.Xr sysctl.conf 5 .
The administrator sets that boot value with an editor or with
.Xr sysconf 8 .
Set
.Va hw.acpi.lid_switch_state
to
.Cm NONE
when closing the lid should default at boot to leaving the machine up.
For a sleep policy, set that sysctl to the name this kernel accepts:
.Cm suspend_to_idle
or
.Cm s2idle ,
or
.Cm fw_suspend
or
.Cm s2mem .
See sysctl
.Va kern.power.supported_stype
for a list of kernel supported policies.
.Cm NONE
means do nothing and is preferred over the
.Va hw.acpi.lid_switch_state
value
.Cm awake .
.Pp
.Ev lid_switchd_switch_state
in
.Xr rc.conf 5
chooses the sleep type
.Cm toggle
writes
.Pq Cm s0ix or Cm s3 .
It does not set the sysctl but rather configures how
.Cm toggle
alters the sysctl
.Pq depending on your kernel .
.Pp
The daemon then listens on a Unix socket so a session can change
the running policy or suspend without becoming root.
.Pp
The socket is mode 0660 and group
.Cm lid_switchd .
The package creates that group.
The daemon refuses to listen when the group is missing.
Add the session account to the group, then log in again so the
new group is in the credentials:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
pw groupmod lid_switchd -m user
.Ed
.Pp
.Xr lid-policy 1
uses the socket to send
.Cm awake ,
.Cm s0ix ,
.Cm s3 ,
and
.Cm toggle
to the root service the rc script started.
One command per connection, one line back.
The same words on the
.Nm
command line require the super-user and act directly.
.Cm awake
sets
.Cm NONE .
.Cm s0ix
sets suspend-to-idle
.Pq Cm suspend_to_idle or Cm s2idle
and makes that the sleep type
.Cm toggle
writes.
.Cm s3
sets firmware suspend
.Pq Cm fw_suspend or Cm s2mem
and makes that the sleep type
.Cm toggle
writes.
.Cm toggle
flips between
.Cm NONE
and that sleep type.
.Cm awake
does not change which sleep type
.Cm toggle
writes.
Each of these changes the running value of
.Va hw.acpi.lid_switch_state
and replies with that value.
They do not rewrite
.Xr rc.conf 5 .
.Cm status
replies with the current value.
.Pp
A suspend-to-idle reply is
.Cm suspend_to_idle
or
.Cm s2idle .
A firmware-suspend reply is
.Cm fw_suspend
or
.Cm s2mem .
Which word appears depends on the kernel.
A script that reads the reply should accept both names of a type.
It does not need the kernel version or
.Va kern.power.supported_stype .
.Pp
.Cm suspend-s0ix
sets
.Va kern.power.suspend
to the same type,
runs
.Xr zzz 8 ,
then restores the previous suspend value.
.Cm suspend-s3
runs
.Xr acpiconf 8
.Fl s Cm 3 .
Those two reply
.Cm ok
or
.Cm error .
.Cm quit
replies
.Cm bye
and the daemon exits.
.Pp
Enable the service with
.Dl sysrc lid_switchd_enable=YES
and start it with
.Dl service lid-switchd start
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "lid_switchd_switch_state"
.It Ev lid_switchd_switch_state
Sleep type
.Cm toggle
writes when the lid state is
.Cm NONE .
.Cm s0ix
is the default and selects suspend-to-idle.
.Cm s3
selects firmware suspend.
.Cm s0ix
and
.Cm s3
on the socket change this for the running service.
The value is read at start and is not rewritten.
.It Ev lid_switchd_socket
Control socket.
The default is
.Pa /var/run/lid-switchd.sock .
.It Ev lid_switchd_group
Socket group.
The default is
.Cm lid_switchd .
The package creates that group.
Any other name must already exist.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "@PREFIX@/etc/rc.d/lid-switchd"
.It Pa @PREFIX@/etc/rc.d/lid-switchd
The rc script.
.It Pa @PREFIX@/sbin/lid-switchd
The daemon.
.It Pa /var/run/lid-switchd.sock
The control socket.
.It Pa /var/run/lid-switchd.pid
The process id.
.It Pa /etc/rc.conf
.Ev lid_switchd_switch_state ,
the sleep type
.Cm toggle
uses.
The daemon does not rewrite this file.
.It Pa /etc/sysctl.conf
Initial value of
.Va hw.acpi.lid_switch_state
.Pq stay awake, or the sleep type .
The daemon does not read or rewrite this file.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Cm serve
runs until
.Cm quit
or a signal.
A missing group, a failure to read the current lid state, or a
failure to bind the socket exits non-zero.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bhotkeys 1 ,
.Xr lid-policy 1 ,
.Xr sysctl.conf 5 ,
.Xr acpiconf 8 ,
.Xr sysconf 8 ,
.Xr zzz 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Devin Teske Aq Mt dteske@FreeBSD.org
